<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Auto-backup rules for API 30 and below (@xml/data_extraction_rules covers 31+).
  Both files must agree; a device on either side of the split should restore the
  same way.

  Two things are deliberately kept out of the backup.

  axiom_secure_prefs — SecureKeyStore's EncryptedSharedPreferences. Its MasterKey
  lives in the Android Keystore, which is never included in a backup. Restoring
  the file onto a device whose Keystore does not hold that key produces a blob
  nothing can decrypt, and EncryptedSharedPreferences.create() throws on open.
  An absent key file means "reconnect your key"; a present, undecryptable one
  means a crash on launch. So: never back it up.

  axiom_database — Room runs in WAL mode, so the durable state at any instant is
  spread across axiom_database, -wal and -shm. Auto-backup takes no database
  lock and can capture the main file without the matching write-ahead log,
  which restores as a journal that is quietly missing its most recent entries.
  Axiom already ships a first-class encrypted export (see BackupScreen), which
  checkpoints properly and which the user controls. A silent partial restore is
  worse than an honest empty start plus a restore prompt.

  What is left to back up is the DataStore in axiom_user_prefs: theme, companion
  name, check-in time, chosen vendor. Losing those is a mild annoyance; restoring
  them is free and cannot corrupt anything.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="axiom_secure_prefs.xml" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="axiom_database" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="axiom_database-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="axiom_database-shm" />
</full-backup-content>
